# Footnotes

Use [Material footnotes](https://squidfunk.github.io/mkdocs-material/reference/footnotes/) for a short aside on one word or sentence. The `footnotes` extension and `content.footnote.tooltips` are enabled, so the note also shows when the marker is hovered.

A reference is `[^id]` with no space before the brackets. The definition uses the same id and can sit anywhere in the file. It always renders at the bottom of the page, with a link back to the reference.

```markdown
A bare number is a width in millimetres.[^mm]

[^mm]: A value like `"50%"` is a percentage of the available width.
```

- Put every definition at the end of the file so the page source stays readable.
- Keep a footnote on one line: `[^mm]: A value like...`
- A longer note starts on the next line, indented four spaces.
- Use a short name for the id, as in `[^mm]`, so the reference is obvious in the source.
- Prefer an admonition when the reader must see the note without leaving the paragraph.
